# Where the `@skema` scope comes from.
#
# The two packages this extension builds against live in different projects of
# the skema-language group - `@skema/model` is published by
# skema-language/skema, `@skema/diagram` by skema-language/skema-lib - and a
# project-level registry endpoint only ever serves its own project. The *group*
# endpoint resolves across every project in the group, so this one line covers
# the whole scope no matter which repo a package came from.
#
# 141817046 is the skema-language group. It is public, so installing needs no
# token - CI included. If a project is ever made private, CI jobs need an auth
# line for this endpoint (see .gitlab-ci.yml) and that project has to allow this
# one under Settings -> CI/CD -> Job token permissions.
@skema:registry=https://gitlab.com/api/v4/groups/141817046/-/packages/npm/
